Rule 9 (if the first input is a list or tuple of integers, its length must match the first dimension of the second input tensor, and the tensor must have a compatible boolean or numeric dtype)
{v_1 : list(int) ⊎ tuple(int), v_2 : tensor} |= v_1.len = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
